{number: 65}
{title: Jesus Is Tenderly Calling}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Jesus is tenderly calling thee home,
Calling today, calling to-[G7] day;
Why [C] from the sunshine of love wilt thou roam,
Farther and [G7] farther a-[C] way?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G7] Calling today, [C] calling today,
[C] Jesus is calling, is [G7] tenderly calling to-[C] day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Jesus is calling the weary to rest,
Calling today, calling to-[G7] day;
Bring [C] Him thy burden, and thou shalt be blest;
He will not [G7] turn thee a-[C] way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Jesus is waiting, oh, come to Him now,
Waiting today, waiting to-[G7] day;
Come [C] with thy sins, at His feet lowly bow;
Come, and no [G7] longer de-[C] lay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Jesus is pleading, oh, list to His voice,
Hear Him today, hear Him to-[G7] day;
They [C] who believe on His name shall rejoice;
Quickly a-[G7] rise and a-[C] way.
{end_of_verse}
